      "cardio"
    ],
    "rotation": [],
    "class": "Cardiac glycoside",
    "class_members": [
      "digoxin"
    ],
    "mechanism": "Inhibits the sodium-potassium ATPase (Na/K ATPase) in heart muscle. Intracellular sodium rises, so the sodium-calcium exchanger removes less calcium, and more calcium is available for contraction. It also raises vagal tone, slowing the AV node.",
    "pharmacokinetics": [
      "cleared by the kidneys, so the dose is cut in kidney disease",
      "narrow therapeutic range",
      "long half-life of about 36 to 48 hours"
    ],
    "indications": [
      "rate control in atrial fibrillation, especially with heart failure",
      "symptom control in heart failure with reduced ejection fraction"
    ],
    "adverse_effects": [
      "nausea, vomiting and abdominal pain",
      "yellow-green vision (xanthopsia) or blurred vision",
      "confusion",
      "arrhythmias of almost any kind, classically atrial tachycardia with block or bidirectional ventricular tachycardia",
      "hyperkalemia in acute overdose"
    ],
    "contraindications": [
      "atrial fibrillation with Wolff-Parkinson-White syndrome",
      "second- or third-degree AV block",
      "hypertrophic obstructive cardiomyopathy"
    ],
    "interactions": [
      "hypokalemia, hypomagnesemia and hypercalcemia increase toxicity",
      "amiodarone, verapamil and quinidine raise digoxin levels",
      "loop and thiazide diuretics cause hypokalemia, which increases toxicity"
    ],
    "monitoring": [
      "digoxin level",
      "potassium and kidney function"
    ],
    "overdose": {
      "features": [
        "nausea and vomiting",
        "visual changes",
        "arrhythmias",
        "hyperkalemia"
      ],
      "treatment": [
        "digoxin-specific antibody fragments (DigiFab)",
        "correct potassium and magnesium"
      ]
    },
    "confused_with": [],
    "pearls": [
      "In acute digoxin poisoning, hyperkalemia predicts death and is an indication for antibody fragments.",
      "Digoxin improves symptoms and cuts hospitalizations in heart failure but does not lower mortality.",
      "Scooped ST segments (the Salvador Dali sag) on the ECG are a digoxin effect, not toxicity."
    ],
